## Generic Arrays

Finally, functions can define generic arrays by combining generic types with generic number of axes, as follow:
```
func Add[T dtype.Floats](a T, b [___S]T) [S___]T
```

```code:main
package main

import "dtype"

func Add[T dtype.Floats](a T, b [___S]T) [S___]T {
    return a+b
}

func Main() ([1][2]float32, [2][3]float32) {
    a := Add(-10, [1][2]float32{{1, 2}})
    b := Add(10, [2][3]float32{{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}})
    return a, b
}
```
